userStories.description:
**Goal** — Carry user images and model input capabilities through nax-ai's public vocabulary, catalog and pi wire boundary.

**Motivation** — pi-ai 1.4.0 already serializes `ImageContent` (`{ type: "image", data, mimeType }`) inside `UserMessage.content`, so the provider-specific work is done. Only nax's own layers need the plumbing.

**Approach** — Images ride **beside** the text, not instead of it: role `user` keeps `content: string` and gains optional `images`. Every existing reader of user `content` (titles, ledgers, prompt audit, the ACP handoff, history replay) keeps working unchanged, and only the layers that talk to a model or to disk learn about images. (The design doc §6.1 proposed a `string | parts[]` union with a `userText` sweep; this side field reaches the same wire shape with no sweep. Recorded in the design doc's decision log.)

`toPiMessages` maps a user message with a non-empty `images` to `{ role: "user", content: [...images.map((i) => ({ type: "image", data: i.data, mimeType: i.mimeType })), ...(content === "" ? [] : [{ type: "text", text: content }])], timestamp }`. `width`, `height` and `source` never reach pi-ai. A user message with no `images`, or an empty one, maps exactly as today (`content` as a string).

nax-ai `ResolvedModel` and `RawModel` gain `input?: readonly ("text" | "image")[]` (absent = unknown, treated as text only). `defaultProviders()` copies pi-ai's `model.input`. `normaliseCatalog` copies `RawModel.input`; when a `ProviderOverride` model declares no `input` and replaces an entry that already has one (same provider and id), the override's resolved model keeps that entry's `input`. A pi model synthesised from an override uses the override's `input` when declared, else today's behaviour (the template's `input` on the bundled-provider path, `["text"]` on the introduced-provider path).

**Scope** — In: protocols/types.ts, protocols/pi-client.ts, providers/types.ts, providers/catalog.ts, providers/pi-catalog.ts; export only the ImageAttachment type from src/index.ts; new test/protocols/pi-client-images.test.ts and relevant catalog/override tests. Out: nax-agent validation/facade/native/storage (US-002–008), ACP client (US-009), nax config (US-010). `ResolvedModel.input` for a new model id introduced on a bundled provider by a `ProviderOverride` that declares no `input`: the resolved model has no `input` (so `imageInput` reports `false`) even though pi model synthesis inherits the template's `input`. Such a model must declare `input` to accept images. Verifying that pi-ai's openai-codex path sends user images is out of scope. Image output from tools: the Read tool, MCP image results (still `[image omitted: <mime>]`), screenshots.

**Interface** — The single image type is nax-ai's `ImageAttachment`:
```ts
export interface ImageAttachment {
  /** One of IMAGE_MIME_TYPES (nax-agent). */
  readonly mimeType: string;
  /** Base64 of the raw image bytes. */
  readonly data: string;
  readonly width?: number;
  readonly height?: number;
  /** Where the image came from ("clipboard", an absolute path, a repo path). Display only; never sent to a model. */
  readonly source?: string;
}

export type ConversationMessage =
  | { readonly role: "user"; readonly content: string; readonly images?: readonly ImageAttachment[] }
  | /* assistant and tool-result members unchanged */;
```
`ResolvedModel` and `RawModel`: `readonly input?: readonly ("text" | "image")[]`. Keep unknown optional fields absent under exactOptionalPropertyTypes. Use existing pi stream/model seams in Vitest; new image tests must not grow the oversized pi-client.test.ts. Preserve the existing orphan tool-result refusal from pi-client.ts:190-193 when an image-bearing user message precedes an unmatched toolCallId; this is an unchanged error-path regression, not new tool-output image support. Show regression tests failing on old code; scripted events prove mapping, not real provider behavior.
